.Dd November 29, 2020
.Dt SOWON 6
.Os AUXILIARY
.Sh NAME
.Nm sowon
.Nd Starting soon timer
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl pe
.Op Ar seconds | Ar clock
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a graphical countdown/timer program.
With no arguments provided, it starts in ascending mode. With an amount of
seconds provided, it starts in descending mode. Accepts human readable time
intervals (1h23m54s). Clock starts it in clock mode, that displays
the current time.
.br
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl p
start in paused state
.It Fl e
exit the application when the countdown ends
.Sh KEY BINDINGS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It SPACE
Toggle pause
.It =
Zoom in
.It -
Zoom out
.It 0
Zoom 100%
.It F5
Restart
.It F11
Fullscreen
.Sh CAT GUARD
When running under the Sway compositor, click the CAT GUARD button to disable
all keyboards by input ID. Click PAWS OFF! to restore them. The keyboard is
also restored by an independent watchdog when a Sway output powers off,
swaylock starts, the session reports LockedHint=yes, or Sowon exits.
Detection takes about one second and leaves CAT GUARD off until manually enabled.
This feature requires swaymsg, jq, and pgrep. Session lock detection additionally
uses loginctl when available.
.Sh FILES
.Pa /usr/local/bin/sowon
